I'm going to have to give up managing the NetHack FAQ.  This Monday's
publication will be the last for me.  I'll still follow the newsgroup,
but corporate policy changes will keep me from FAQ publication.

The post of FAQ publisher is therefore up for grabs.  If you would like
the job, no special skills beyond arranging for posting are required.
People will send you e-mail when things change and the FAQ needs
correction.  Rarely, a discussion of proposed changes may occur here
in r.g.h.

To become the FAQ publisher, you need to do two things:

    1) be the first to post a follow-on article that says "MINE! MINE!"

    2) grab a recent copy of the FAQ from r.g.h. and set it up for
       publication on a fairly regular basis.  I've been posting
       it twice-weekly, but that's because the automated tool
       I use would not let me use "Expires:" or "Supercedes:" flags.

The FAQ publisher should expect to receive approximately 2 E-mail requests
per week for assistance or clarification.

It was easy taking over for Dave, as he built the basic model and I only
made minor changes.  It should therefore be fairly easy taking over for me,
too.

Thanks in advance to whoever volunteers!
